**Issue**: The RAF loop runs continuously even when the user isn't scrolling. Lenis is a smooth scroll library — it only needs RAF when actively scrolling. With `autoRaf: false`, you're manually driving RAF continuously.

**Fix**: Lenis has a built-in auto-RAF mode. Enable it instead:

```jsx
<ReactLenis root ref={lenisRef} options={{ autoRaf: true }}>
  {/* Remove the manual RAF effect entirely */}
```

